# The twelfth tooling step's third part: CI and measurement.

# `try --final`: one run of three jobs.

[break] final-tests-part-compares-too
rule: A final run's Linux 22.04 job runs the tests alone: only the Windows job is an A/B.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: for_part
find: "tests" => inputs.words = vec!["test".to_owned()],
replace: "tests" => { inputs.words = vec!["test".to_owned()]; inputs.against = self.against.clone(); }
caught-by:
    try_run::tests::a_final_runs_job_runs_the_part_it_is_given_and_nothing_else
    try_run::tests::a_final_dry_run_shows_each_of_its_three_jobs_and_what_it_runs

[break] final-ab-loses-its-count
rule: A final run's count is the rounds of its A/B.
